"""Niche-specific reviews for home communication and workplace systems."""

from review_angle_plans import audit, revise_domain


COMMUNICATION = """history_origins|How a Household Message Changed|How did one household's way of coordinating care change with a new medium?|Compare dated accounts of face-to-face, phone, and messaging practice.
famous_examples|A Popular Communication Method Tested|Does one widely recommended conversation technique help in a defined setting?|Check the original evidence and outcomes, avoiding universal prescriptions.
hidden_stories|Who Carries the Message?|Who translates, reminds, and mediates communication within one household?|Use consented accounts and time-use evidence without exposing private disputes.
beginner_explainers|Message, Meaning, and Feedback|How can two people understand the same request differently?|Use an anonymized example to distinguish wording, context, response, and repair.
advanced_concepts|Power in a Conversation|How does dependence or authority affect whether a household member can speak?|Analyze one bounded setting with privacy and safety protections.
mysteries_unsolved_cases|Why a Message Failed|Which competing explanations fit a missed household instruction?|Check channel, timing, assumptions, language, and access without blaming one person.
technology_innovation|A Group Chat at Home|How does a shared messaging tool change coordination and privacy?|Compare who gains access, notification load, recordkeeping, and exclusion.
people_personalities|The Family Translator|What burden falls on a person who interprets for relatives?|Use consented testimony and service-access context, especially for minors.
major_events|Communication During a Household Crisis|Which messages helped people coordinate during one documented disruption?|Use anonymized timelines; avoid revealing sensitive locations or identities.
how_it_works|A Household Decision Meeting|How do members share information and reach a decision about one shared task?|Map roles, options, follow-up, and who could dissent.
rise_fall|Why a Routine Stopped Working|What changed when one household communication habit broke down?|Compare time demands, living arrangements, and members' accounts.
then_vs_now|Keeping in Touch Across Generations|How did one family's communication change after migration or new technology?|Compare consented accounts and available channels across dates.
future_developments|Choosing a Better Shared Channel|What would make a proposed household coordination method workable?|Check accessibility, privacy, costs, and members' preferences before adoption.
myths_vs_facts|The Screen-Time Blame Story|Does evidence support a claim that one device caused poorer family communication?|Define outcome, comparator, and other changes before inferring cause.
documentary_stories|A Care Plan's Communication Trail|How was one shared care plan understood and revised among participants?|Use consented records, dates, and roles without revealing medical details.
lived_experience|A Misunderstood Request|What does one person's account show about communication barriers at home?|Pair an anonymized account with context; do not diagnose relationships.
institutional_pathway|When Outside Services Contact Home|How does school, clinic, or housing communication reach every household member?|Trace language, channel, timing, and consent in one service pathway.
incentives_norms|Why People Say Yes and Mean Maybe|How do household norms affect agreement and follow-through?|Compare spoken commitments with practical constraints and cultural context.
access_and_exclusion|Who Misses the Update?|Which household members are excluded by a chosen communication channel?|Test language, hearing, vision, literacy, device, and schedule access.
community_variation|Different Ways to Share Decisions|How do communication practices vary across specific households or communities?|Use bounded participant accounts without ranking cultures.
policy_in_practice|A New Notice Rule at Home|Did a school or service communication rule actually reach households?|Compare intended recipients, delivery data, and consented experiences.
survey_vs_story|What Survey Answers Miss|Do reported communication frequencies describe how households coordinate?|Compare a defined survey item with interview accounts and sampling limits.
power_and_voice|Who Gets to Set the Agenda?|How are voices weighted in one household decision?|Examine resources, care roles, and safe opportunities to disagree.
unintended_consequence|A Helpful Reminder Becomes a Burden|Did a new messaging routine increase pressure on one member?|Compare tasks and expectations before and after with consented accounts.
comparative_setting|Same Request, Different Channel|Does face-to-face, paper, or digital communication change understanding?|Compare one defined message and accessible outcome measures.
change_over_time|A Conversation Habit Evolves|How did a household adapt communication after a change in work or living space?|Use dates, member perspectives, and practical constraints.
ethical_dilemma|Privacy Versus Shared Information|Who should receive sensitive household information needed for care?|Frame consent, autonomy, safety, and local rules without personal advice.
field_space_constraints|Talking in Crowded Space|How does lack of private space affect one household conversation?|Use anonymized observations and residents' interpretations.
field_household_cost|The Cost of Staying Connected|Which phone, data, travel, or time costs limit contact?|Compare actual costs and access across members.
field_design_for_access|Making a Message Accessible|Which format helps a defined household understand one notice?|Test translated, audio, visual, and plain-language versions with users.
field_maintenance_burden|Keeping a Shared System Current|Who updates calendars, contacts, and care instructions?|Track ongoing time and handoff failures, not just initial setup.
field_material_lifecycle|Paper and Devices at Home|How do paper notes and devices age or disappear in a household system?|Follow loss, replacement, privacy, and disposal in one case."""


LEADERSHIP = """history_origins|Where a Management Practice Came From|What problem did one named management method originally address?|Trace its source, setting, evidence, and later reinterpretations.
famous_examples|A Celebrated Leader's Record|Which outcomes can fairly be attributed to one leader's decisions?|Compare team baseline, collaborators, constraints, and counterevidence.
hidden_stories|Who Made the Strategy Work?|Whose labor is missing from a leader-centered success story?|Trace implementation through staff roles and attributed accounts.
beginner_explainers|What Does a Manager Decide?|Which decisions belong to a manager, team, or institution?|Map authority, delegation, accountability, and appeal in one workplace.
advanced_concepts|Incentives and Trust|How can a target improve one metric while damaging another?|Compare intended measures, workarounds, and worker outcomes.
mysteries_unsolved_cases|Why the Team Missed a Goal|Which plausible causes explain one project's failure?|Compare staffing, resources, market changes, and decision records.
technology_innovation|A Dashboard for Managers|Did a new reporting tool improve decisions or increase surveillance?|Compare accuracy, use, privacy, worker input, and outcomes.
people_personalities|A Leader's Choice Under Pressure|What options and evidence did a named manager have at one decision point?|Use dated records and staff perspectives, avoiding mind-reading.
major_events|Management During a Shock|How did one team reorganize after a documented disruption?|Trace decisions, communication, workload, and worker effects.
how_it_works|From Goal to Team Work|How are priorities translated into assignments and feedback?|Observe one planning cycle, authority, resources, and revision.
rise_fall|A Management Fad Fades|Why did one method lose support in a specific organization?|Compare promised outcomes, measured results, costs, and alternatives.
then_vs_now|The Manager's Role Changes|How did one occupation's management duties change across two periods?|Compare authority, staffing, technology, and labor rules.
future_developments|Piloting a New Team Structure|What would demonstrate whether a proposed structure improves work?|Define baseline, worker participation, measures, and stopping rules.
myths_vs_facts|The Hero CEO Story|Does evidence support sole-leader credit for one turnaround?|Compare decisions, timing, staff work, market conditions, and predecessor plans.
documentary_stories|One Decision's Paper Trail|How did a leadership decision move from proposal to workplace practice?|Build a dated chain of meetings, objections, implementation, and review.
lived_experience|Managed From Below|How did one employee experience a management change?|Pair a consented account with policy and team-level evidence.
institutional_pathway|Escalating a Concern|Where does an employee's concern go within one management structure?|Map channels, decision authority, response times, and retaliation safeguards.
incentives_norms|What a Bonus Actually Rewards|How did one incentive alter decisions or collaboration?|Compare formal criteria, observed behavior, and unintended effects.
access_and_exclusion|Who Gets Stretch Assignments?|Which rules or informal choices shape access to leadership opportunities?|Compare assignment records with worker accounts and role requirements.
community_variation|One Method Across Teams|Why did a management practice work differently across two teams?|Compare resources, autonomy, task type, and team composition.
policy_in_practice|Did a Feedback Rule Work?|Did a new feedback policy change actual conversations and outcomes?|Compare participation, quality, and follow-up before and after.
survey_vs_story|The Engagement Score and Staff Accounts|What can a survey establish about one team's management?|Check response rate, question wording, and confidential interviews.
power_and_voice|Who Can Challenge a Decision?|How can team members safely disagree with a manager?|Examine formal appeals, informal norms, and documented consequences.
unintended_consequence|A Target With Side Effects|Did a productivity target shift hidden work or risk to staff?|Compare metrics with service quality, overtime, and worker reports.
comparative_setting|Two Teams, Two Decision Systems|How do centralized and delegated decisions affect one task?|Compare matched teams, authority, speed, errors, and worker experience.
change_over_time|A New Manager's First Year|Which changes persisted after a manager's arrival?|Use dated outcomes and preexisting trends, not a before-after story alone.
ethical_dilemma|The Deadline and Staff Capacity|How should a manager weigh delivery against workload and safety?|Present documented constraints, duties, alternatives, and affected views.
field_skill_signals|What Predicts Management Skill?|Which evidence shows a candidate can coordinate and support a team?|Compare job-relevant work samples with later outcomes and bias risks.
field_hiring_filters|Selecting a Manager|Which hiring screen excludes qualified candidates?|Review criteria, applicant flow, validation, and appeal.
field_workplace_power|Managing With Authority|How does control over schedules or pay affect honest feedback?|Use confidential evidence and safeguard worker identities.
field_career_transitions|From Specialist to Manager|Which supports help someone move into a people-management role?|Compare training, workload, mentoring, and worker feedback.
field_worker_support|Support After a Management Change|Which resources helped staff adapt to new demands?|Check actual access, uptake, workload, and sustained outcomes."""


WORKPLACE = """history_origins|How This Workplace Was Organized|Why did one firm's work arrangement emerge?|Trace production needs, labor rules, technology, and worker negotiations.
famous_examples|A Famous Office Model Tested|Does a celebrated workplace design produce its claimed outcomes?|Compare original aims, representative worker experience, and measured results.
hidden_stories|Invisible Work in the Firm|Which workers keep an office or operation running outside the company story?|Include cleaners, contractors, support staff, and their employment terms.
beginner_explainers|Reading a Workplace Structure|How do employer, contractor, manager, and team roles differ?|Map one organization's actual decision and pay relationships.
advanced_concepts|Efficiency and Risk Transfer|Who saves money and who absorbs risk under one work arrangement?|Compare company costs, wages, stability, and service quality.
mysteries_unsolved_cases|Why Turnover Rose|Which factors might explain a sudden rise in departures?|Compare pay, schedules, leadership, market options, and survey limits.
technology_innovation|Monitoring Work Digitally|How did one tracking system change work, privacy, or bargaining power?|Examine data accuracy, worker consent, use, and outcomes.
people_personalities|Workers Behind a Corporate Change|Who proposed, resisted, and implemented one organizational reform?|Use dated records and voices from multiple job levels.
major_events|A Firm During a Disruption|How did a corporate workplace respond to a dated shock?|Trace staffing, safety, pay, service, and recovery decisions.
how_it_works|A Workday Across Departments|How do tasks move between teams in one organization?|Map handoffs, waiting, rework, and informal labor.
rise_fall|Why a Workplace Model Ended|Which evidence explains the end of one office or staffing model?|Compare costs, performance, worker views, and external changes.
then_vs_now|The Same Job Across Two Eras|How did duties, hours, pay, and control change for one role?|Use comparable job records and worker accounts.
future_developments|A New Work Arrangement Proposal|What would show whether a hybrid or flexible policy works?|Define eligibility, output, equity, costs, and review dates.
myths_vs_facts|The Productivity Claim Checked|Does one firm's claim about a work arrangement match its evidence?|Check baseline, metrics, selection, and who is omitted.
documentary_stories|A Corporate Policy's Journey|How did one workplace policy move from announcement to daily practice?|Build a timeline of drafting, consultation, training, use, and revision.
lived_experience|One Worker, One Policy|What did an employee actually encounter under a company rule?|Use consented account and records without treating it as universal.
institutional_pathway|Resolving a Workplace Complaint|Which steps take a worker concern from report to remedy?|Map confidentiality, authority, deadlines, protections, and outcomes.
incentives_norms|The Rule Versus the Real Work|Why do workers follow an informal routine instead of a formal procedure?|Compare task pressure, training, incentives, and safety effects.
access_and_exclusion|Who Can Use Flexibility?|Which job or eligibility rules limit access to flexible work?|Compare roles, care needs, disability access, and actual uptake.
community_variation|Work Across Sites|Why does the same company policy feel different at two locations?|Compare management, labor market, facilities, and worker representation.
policy_in_practice|Does the Leave Policy Reach Workers?|Can eligible workers actually take the leave on offer?|Compare rules, awareness, staffing cover, pay, and take-up.
survey_vs_story|Engagement Numbers in Context|What do staff surveys miss about conditions at work?|Assess nonresponse, question wording, job categories, and confidential accounts.
power_and_voice|Worker Voice in Decisions|Where can employees influence scheduling, safety, or restructuring?|Compare consultation rights with actual decision records and outcomes.
unintended_consequence|A Cost Saving's Hidden Burden|Did a cost cut move work to unpaid time or contractors?|Trace hours, quality, safety, and contract terms before and after.
comparative_setting|Two Sites, One Policy|Does one policy have different effects across comparable workplaces?|Use matched measures and explain contextual differences.
change_over_time|A Workplace After Restructuring|Which outcomes changed over several periods after a reorganization?|Compare staffing, pay, output, and preexisting trends.
ethical_dilemma|Disclosure Before a Layoff|How should a firm handle uncertainty when jobs may be cut?|Examine legal duties, confidentiality, timing, and worker consequences.
field_skill_signals|What a Job Description Signals|Do stated qualifications match the tasks actually performed?|Compare postings, work observation, pay bands, and worker accounts.
field_hiring_filters|A Hiring Funnel Under Review|At which stage are applicants lost, and why?|Check job relevance, accessibility, selection data, and appeal routes.
field_workplace_power|Who Controls the Schedule?|How does scheduling authority affect income and family life?|Compare actual notice, changes, pay, and worker voice.
field_career_transitions|Moving Within a Firm|Who can reach training, promotion, or a new role?|Compare criteria, openings, participation, and outcomes across groups.
field_worker_support|Support in Practice|Do announced worker supports reach the people who need them?|Measure eligibility, privacy, uptake, delays, and worker assessments."""


if __name__ == "__main__":
    revise_domain("102", "102_communication", COMMUNICATION,
                  "Everyday communication in households and close relationships through coordination, access, privacy, power, and repair of misunderstandings.",
                  "consented and anonymized participant accounts, household time-use data, service communication records, and applicable accessibility and psychosocial guidance",
                  "Use a defined household setting and protect privacy. Do not diagnose relationships or offer personal counseling; seek current guidance for safety-sensitive cases.")
    revise_domain("103", "103_leadership_management", LEADERSHIP,
                  "Leadership and management as accountable decisions about teams, incentives, work allocation, feedback, and worker support.",
                  "dated decision and policy records, relevant management research, worker surveys with response limits, and confidential attributed accounts",
                  "Name organization, role, jurisdiction, and period. Separate leader claims from measured outcomes, protect employee identity, and check applicable labor rules.")
    revise_domain("104", "104_corporate_workplace", WORKPLACE,
                  "Corporate workplaces as systems of employment, staffing, schedules, policy, worker voice, facilities, and organizational change.",
                  "employment and policy records, representative workforce data, labor standards, workplace surveys, and consented worker accounts",
                  "Name workplace, jurisdiction, worker group, and period. Check labor law and safety obligations, protect vulnerable workers, and separate company claims from observed conditions.")
    rows = audit()
    print(f"Plans: {len(rows)}; reviewed question designs: {sum(r['status'] == 'editorial_question_reviewed' for r in rows)}")
